# Infectious disease surveillance in Chad: a descriptive time-series analysis of case report data, 2014–2025

Analysis code accompanying the manuscript *Infectious disease surveillance 
in Chad: a descriptive time-series analysis of case report data, 2014–2025*.

## Contents

- `02_missing.Rmd` — Assessment of missingness in the national Integrated 
  Disease Surveillance (IDS) case report data. Identifies districts with 
  complete or near-complete missingness used as placeholders by the 
  surveillance team, and districts activated mid-year.

Additional scripts covering data cleaning, analysis, and figure generation 
will be added as the manuscript is finalised.

## Data availability

The data reported in this Article are stored in a non-publicly available 
repository at the Yale School of Public Health. All datasets belong to the 
Ministry of Health of Chad. Researchers who would like to access these 
datasets can submit a request to the corresponding author. All requests 
must be approved by the Ministry of Health of Chad. Researchers given 
access to the data will sign data sharing agreements which will restrict 
the use to answering pre-specified research questions.

Because the underlying data are not included, the analyses in this 
repository are not directly reproducible. The code is provided so that 
the methods described in the manuscript can be inspected and evaluated.

## Requirements

R version 4.4.1.

Scripts use the `here` package for file paths and assume raw data are 
placed in a `data/` directory at the project root.

